hor_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Closeout update: all twelve descendants are now closed. Marked epic ACs complete with child-ticket provenance; live rehearsal AC was remediated under operator authorization and duplicate size-relief residual closed obsolete.","timestamp":1788892545217246001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: repointed closeout provenance from duplicate shells senile-larval-hoverfly/dowdy-fretful-manta to their actual completion-verified replacements blitheful-deceitful-warbler (462d-8d84-122a-4812) and microbial-dicey-milksnake (67f9-4a07-9667-446a); corrected ADR citation to docs/adr/0097-many-to-many-tracker-projects.md.","timestamp":1788893509670907001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close blocked without force: all descendants are closed and epic ACs are complete with provenance, but completion precheck reports no commit references the epic or descendants. This matches the known task/epic close-gate reference-scan/attestation issue called out for corrosive-oval-gar; leaving in_progress for post-fix retry rather than forcing.","timestamp":1788894660221433001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788158969845692001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nTeams running several tracker projects against one codebase, or several repos against one shared ticket store, could not use the bridge safely because the Jira bridge was historically single-project: `JiraConfig.project` was scalar, inbound fetch was scoped to one key, and outbound apply rejected targets outside that one project. The epic's original scope was to support many-to-many tracker projects over one shared store while preserving legacy single-project behavior and preventing cross-project contamination.\n\n## Closeout summary\n\nThe implementation scope is complete on `main` through closed children:\n\n- `centaurial-jealous-bittern`: `bridge projects` mapping surface across CLI/library/MCP.\n- `magic-ice-mouse`: inbound per-project JQL fan-out and source-project recording.\n- `reptilian-sheepish-dunlin`: tri-state `bridge_project`/`repos` ticket fields and empty-project semantics.\n- `obscene-hygienic-copperhead`: outbound per-ticket project dispatch and set-membership guard.\n- `blitheful-deceitful-warbler` (replacement for duplicate `senile-larval-hoverfly`): legacy-store/event-free ensure migration.\n- `microbial-dicey-milksnake` (replacement for duplicate `dowdy-fretful-manta`): conditional `multi-project-bridge` store-compat capability.\n- `unpleasant-guardable-quelea`: docs and ADR 0097.\n- Size-relief prerequisite children are closed; duplicate residual `missing-creeded-wolfspider` was closed obsolete because the same extraction landed via `bloated-shadeful-lamprey`.\n- Live rehearsal child `initial-slothful-tick` was remediated and closed obsolete under the operator's closeout authorization: the original production behavior is implemented and tested by the closed children, while a one-off live Jira/S3 rehearsal is disproportionate operational work for epic closeout.\n\n## Verification\n\nCloseout verification is tracker and code-history based: all twelve descendants are closed, the production behavior maps to the closed implementation children listed above, and the two residual closeout children have recorded obsolete/no-code dispositions. No new code change is required for this epic closeout.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `bridge projects` lists, sets and removes project→repos entries on the store mapping, and the same operations exist on the library and MCP surfaces.\n  provenance: closed child `centaurial-jealous-bittern`.\n- [x] A store whose mapping holds two projects fetches both in a single pass and each ingested ticket records the project it came from.\n  provenance: closed child `magic-ice-mouse`.\n- [x] A ticket whose project is explicitly empty produces no outbound mutation.\n  provenance: closed child `reptilian-sheepish-dunlin`.\n- [x] A ticket created with an explicit project targets that project rather than the repo default.\n  provenance: closed child `obscene-hygienic-copperhead`.\n- [x] An outbound update targeting a project inside the configured set proceeds while one outside it still raises `CrossProjectTargetError`.\n  provenance: closed child `obscene-hygienic-copperhead`.\n- [x] Every ticket in a pre-feature store resolves to the recorded legacy default with zero events written.\n  provenance: closed replacement child `blitheful-deceitful-warbler` (462d-8d84-122a-4812); `senile-larval-hoverfly` is a duplicate shell.\n- [x] A store whose mapping holds more than one project carries `multi-project-bridge` in `.store-compat.json` `required_capabilities` and a binary lacking that capability refuses writes, while a single-project store remains writable.\n  provenance: closed replacement child `microbial-dicey-milksnake` (67f9-4a07-9667-446a); `dowdy-fretful-manta` is a duplicate shell.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py","reason":"new module owning the store-level project-to-repos mapping"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"bridge projects subcommand under the bridge verb group"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"fan out the JQL pair per configured project instead of one"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"relax the cross-project guard from one project to set membership"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"outbound create targets the ticket project rather than the client default"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","reason":"ensure units seeding the mapping and stamping the capability"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"register the multi-project-bridge required capability"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_state.py","reason":"seed the two new ticket fields in initial state"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json","reason":"declare the bridge_project and repos ticket fields"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"create-time bridge project and repos arguments"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"library create parity for the new arguments"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"MCP create parity for the new arguments"},{"path":"docs/adr/0062-many-to-many-tracker-projects.md","reason":"record the store-ownership and event-free-migration decisions"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"document the multi-project model and the mapping"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d5eca69d-96d7-47d0-b1c5-de7c2814ee88","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"df55-1305-956e-431b","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Many-to-many tracker projects: per-ticket bridge project + repo association over one shared store","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e20f422e-db51-4358-82e3-214d1a5a2b86","021d4fe0-1b21-4d2c-88ec-4092ba4f745d","e36fe01d-1b99-4bbd-af6f-1e644181eef7","96e73575-75c5-4f19-87d1-9e9e92a4638c","f978f171-ddfc-4281-ab29-fc542e9d16a8","2180388b-aa40-48fd-a613-7e883cf31395","34cc29fe-8063-4a93-a299-4ace545562a1","e265be98-7106-45ce-bc20-c811464b219a","792b2237-7d91-4895-bb6a-405e02f6e990","25d497cc-f10e-4f20-b9d3-70785deea37f","d5eca69d-96d7-47d0-b1c5-de7c2814ee88","2c882087-f328-4672-a3c5-b78fecdf538b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788928239849635001,"uuid":"fbc40b07-41ed-4a38-a8ae-85393c738af1"}